  "facts": [
    "The 145th Street Bridge, designed by Alfred Pancoast Boller, opened on August 24, 1905, after construction began on April 19, 1901, and was built to accommodate growing water traffic by modifying the Macombs Dam Bridge design.",
    "In 1957, the bridge received approach spans over Harlem River Drive, and in 1990, three additional spans were added to grant the Oak Point Link railway a right‑of‑way, showcasing its evolving infrastructure.",
    "A brand‑new swing span, assembled in Coeymans, New York, arrived in 2006 and replaced the old section in February 2007, modernizing the bridge while preserving its historic swing mechanism."
